    "index_exact_complete_anchor": "    <a href=\"/static/common-suggestions.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Common saved suggestions (new tab)</a>\n",
    "index_receipt_fragment_explanation": "The earlier inverse insertion receipt used longest common prefix/suffix inside repeated link text. Root directly read the actual complete valid anchor and independently removed exactly its 116 bytes to recover the original index; no product defect or repair.",
    "findings": [
      "API admits exactly two through six dense own-indexed sources; string labels are bounded by UTF-8 bytes and saved text by two MiB before unchanged readWeekFile validation and the 500-pick consumer limit.",
      "JSON string encoding of the kind/id pair gives exact injective string identity. The first source determines group order; all matching duplicate occurrences retain source-index/native order with full snapshots and saved records.",
      "No trimming, case folding, Unicode normalization, name matching, inferred suitability, refreshed venue checking or shared-availability computation is introduced.",
      "The new API has no filesystem, network, storage, clock-now or random calls. Explicit saved-date parsing remains in the unchanged original modules. Full-value receiving separately checks frozen inputs, mutation and distinct result object graphs.",
      "UI selection/Clear/Remove generations retire stale results and invalidate late reads; a cancelled chooser is a no-op and a refused replacement preserves the previous accepted source. Pending reads disable comparison.",
      "Browser file size is checked before and after arrayBuffer; fatal UTF-8 decoding with ignoreBOM true preserves one BOM for original codec handling. Malformed/invalid/oversized input is refused through current status.",
      "File-derived display content uses textContent. Source cards and occurrence rows keep saved facts, source mode/week/notes/model messages, duplicates, dates and off-week state visible.",
      "Export is guarded by the current result and uses a fixed basename with UTF-8 JSON, two-space formatting and a final LF. Object URL failure leaves the current result available; temporary link and object URL cleanup is explicit.",
      "Print is guarded by the current result and invokes the existing browser print capability. CSS hides interactive controls and keeps source/result content; narrow layout uses wrapping and visible keyboard focus.",
      "The separate page and guide accurately explain local static serving, limits, saved-data review and absent guarantees. The only existing-file changes are the 464-byte README append and 116-byte anchor insertion."
    ]
